WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.568
Jack Smith and his team are coming out.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.303
So let's listen in.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.344
Good afternoon.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.881
Today, an indictment is unsealed

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.882
charging Donald J.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.951
Trump with felony violations

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.253
of our national security laws,

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.055
as well as participating

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.257
in a conspiracy to obstruct justice.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.327
This indictment was voted by a grand

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.528
jury of citizens

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.630
in the Southern District of Florida.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.333
Now, I invite everyone to read it in full

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.268
to understand the scope

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.571
and the gravity of the crimes charged.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.073
The men and women

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:40.974
of the United States

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:41.975
intelligence community

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.811
and our armed forces dedicate their lives

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.213
to protecting our nation and its people.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.382
Our laws

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.584
that protect national defense information

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.286
are critical

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.087
to the safety

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.656
and security of the United States,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.893
and they must be enforced.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.295
Violations of those laws put our country

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:02.862
at risk.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.833
Adherence to the rule of law

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.268
is a bedrock principle

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.470
of the Department of Justice,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.738
and our nation's commitment

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.173
to the rule of law

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.443
sets an example for the world.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.511
We have one set of laws in this country,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.481
and they apply to everyone

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.883
applying those laws, collecting facts.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.285
That's what determines

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.421
the outcome of an investigation.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.124
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.361
The prosecutors in my office are among

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.430
the most talented

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.398
and experienced

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.567
in the Department of Justice.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.601
They have investigated

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.136
this case, hewing to the highest

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.671
ethical standards,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.872
and they will continue to do

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.641
so in this case proceeds.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.877
It's very important for me to note

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.046
that the defendants in this case

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.881
must be presumed innocent

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.583
until proven guilty

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.551
beyond a reasonable doubt

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.120
in a court of law.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:01.688
To that

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.622
end, my

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.324
office will seek a speedy trial

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.658
in this matter,

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.260
consistent with the public interest

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.330
and the rights of the accused.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.898
We very much look forward

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.466
to presenting our case

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.101
to a jury of citizens

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:17.971
in the Southern District of Florida

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.307
In conclusion, I would like to thank

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.276
the dedicated public

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.878
servants of the Federal Bureau

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.446
of Investigation

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:26.846
with whom

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.114
my office is conducting

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.616
this investigation,

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:32.285
and who work tirelessly every day

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.687
upholding the rule of law in our country.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.790
I'm deeply proud to stand shoulder

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.692
to shoulder with them.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.528
Thank you very much.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.630
Why that?

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.464
Why did you decide

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.066
to bring the case in Florida?

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.536
I was special counsel Jack Smith.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:49.836
We knew

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.104
he wasn't going to take questions,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:51.938
even though

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.039
one eager reporter

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.673
attempted there,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.841
speaking at the Justice Department,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.042
talking about the federal charges

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.810
facing former President Donald Trump

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.645
and one of his aides.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.213
The indictment released this afternoon

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:03.349
detailing 37 charges facing Mr.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.218
Trump, including the willful retention

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.753
of national defense information

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.921
and obstruction of justice.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.456
Let's discuss with my panel.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.124
And Laura Coates,

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:11.691
let me start with you,

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.160
because I want you to translate for us.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.396
When Jack Smith says

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.564
that they are going to pursue

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.532
a speedy trial

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.934
pursuant to all the rights

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.001
that the accused has.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.769
What does that mean?

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.170
How soon might this trial begin?

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.672
Well, he obviously is aware

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.272
that the Department of

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.240
Justice has a policy.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.408
They don't want to do anything

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.443
that might interfere with an election.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.579
We know we are 500 some days away

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.846
from the presidential election

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.380
and two months

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.315
from the first of three months

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.182
from the first debate

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.483
and of course, primaries ahead

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.152
about after as well.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.420
He's aware of that.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.588
And the talking point

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.722
is obviously out there.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.190
And he tried to undermine the idea

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.792
of the adherence to the law

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:46.893
as a bedrock principle

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.361
and nothing else was actually the reason

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.129
to do this. He's aware of that.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.332
And so with an eye towards that notion,

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.067
he is trying to confirm to the people

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:54.801
of the United States

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.269
who are hearing him right now

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.237
that they are going to do

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.771
everything that they can now.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.707
That does not mean that the judge

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.108
or everyone else in this case

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:02.842
will do everything

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.776
that they can

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:04.210
to do this

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.612
before any of those timelines,

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.447
because as you can imagine,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.382
if, for example, Donald Trump

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.316
somehow secures

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.818
the RNC nomination

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.686
and if he is able to become

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.053
the president,

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.288
the United States yet again

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.657
and win over the Democratic incumbent,

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.559
then that would mean that any player

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.060
would actually toll at that point.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.095
Because now that you can no longer

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.663
continue to pursue a case

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.998
against a sitting president

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.499
based on DOJ guidelines,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.501
and so the speed and the timing

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.937
will both be a friend and a foe of Jack

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.438
Smith and Andy McCabe.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.573
Let me ask you,

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.507
as a former FBI

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.308
official, is it

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.210
unusual that the Justice Department

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.712
decided to release the indictment today?

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.748
And if so, why do you think they did?

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:42.849
Highly unusual.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.684
The normal order is the indictment

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.451
remains sealed

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.219
until the defendant

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.820
is presented in court at the arraignment,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.156
which we know Tuesday in Miami.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:50.556
That's right.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.391
Tuesday in Miami

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.726
about about the same time we're at today.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.795
So that's how it normally happens.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.929
I'm a little bit surprised

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:57.697
that they released it

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:58.331
early here

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.565
simply because

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.633
I think it would have been

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.801
in their advantage

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.669
to be able to say

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.270
we followed the normal process

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:04.871
with respect

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.906
to this remarkable defendant

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.641
in every possible instance.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.542
However,

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.412
I think that DOJ capitulated in some

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:15.548
some respect to the enormous pressure

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:16.916
that's been put on them by

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:17.850
we in the media

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.952
and some political figures saying like,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.454
this thing is so volatile,

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.722
people are so interested in it,

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.790
and the American people

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.291
need to see these facts today.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.259
So that's what they did.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.927
But this press conference, very clearly,

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.662
this was like a cover letter, right?

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.664
There was no substance here.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.433
What Jack Smith wants us to do

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.500
is read the indictment,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.635
and he started his comments

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.669
by saying exactly

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.738
that we have one set of laws

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:39.839
protecting information

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:40.773
for national security

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.375
sake is incredibly important.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.876
And read the indictment.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:44.777
And that's basically all you.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:45.678
Dana Bash,

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.580
a lot of the Republicans

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.515
out there running for president

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.583
against Donald Trump,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.085
with the exceptions of Chris Christie.

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:53.252
And these are Hutchinson,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:53.853
a lot of them

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.688
running to Donald Trump's defense

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:56.022
You know,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:56.522
and I

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.691
literally just got a text from a

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.426
veteran Republican strategist

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.260
not affiliated

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.795
with any of the presidential campaigns

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.263
saying if a candidate

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.932
can't make an effective argument

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.734
that this guy might very well be in jail.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.669
I don't know what they can do.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.270
Well, they probably won't.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.038
I mean,

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.639
many of the candidates

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.541
I mean, even down to former Vice

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.442
President Mike Pence,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.777
who you were speaking to just

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:18.811
a couple of days ago,

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.414
not wanting to talk about it, really

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:22.949
going out of his way today

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.150
to discuss

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.084
to not discuss

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.153
the substance of this case.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.554
Pence

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.824
is not quite in the Asa Hutchinson camp,

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.726
not quite in the

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:34.761
maybe the Chris Sununu

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.229
or the Chris Christie camp.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.598
But he is staking his campaign

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:39.332
on this

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:42.435
premise that Trump violated his oath

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.337
on January 6th

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:46.606
and should not be president again.

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.874
But he is reluctant,

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.642
it seems, at this very moment.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.777
And that could change in the future,

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.445
but right now is reluctant

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.247
to weigh in on this case.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:55.481
A lot of these candidates,

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.583
a lot of Republicans right now

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.918
probably understand

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.454
what the poll numbers have shown us over

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.956
a long period of time, which is that

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:04.757
at the very least,

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.993
it's probably about half of Republicans

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.594
will are willing to

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.495
or have been willing up

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:09.996
until this point

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:12.131
to give Trump a pass on this case

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.299
and on many others.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.066
Will that change

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.301
based on this indictment?

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:15.968
We don't know.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.537
But a lot of Republicans in the field

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:18.337
right now

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.105
are looking to see

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:20.072
where the wind is blowing

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.474
to determine where they go.

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.175
And not enough

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.676
time has passed as of right now.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:24.010
Jamie,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.812
I would just say beyond reluctant,

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:27.814
I mean, we saw Pence

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:29.615
come out with his announcement

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.751
and finally say these things.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.520
On the other hand, he also said he did

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.122
not think charges

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:38.658
should be pursued against Trump.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:39.058
Right.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.660
No one should be above the law,

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.828
but don't do this.

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:42.829
So let's let's talk a little bit

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.497
about the substance. If we can.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.666
John, we'll talk to former Governor

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:48.201
Asa Hutchinson later in the show.

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:49.535
He's actually calling for Donald Trump

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:50.570
to drop out of the race

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.637
because of this indictment.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.673
I mean, when you read the indictment,

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:54.907
it's stunning

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.909
and it's entirely credible

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.044
because it's based on

00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:01.280
contemporaneous notes, texts, photographs

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:02.648
and transcripts

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.350
and the detail in it is stunning.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.651
And also important to note,

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.053
when you craft an indictment,

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.221
the lawyers can say this better

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.855
than I do.

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.623
You want to prove your case.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.492
Probable cause to make the count.

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:13.893
There's a lot in there.

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.027
It's also a lot that's not in there.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.462
You don't have to put it all in there.

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:17.730
And so what they put in there,

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.464
Trump's conversation

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:19.298
with his lawyers, text

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.733
messages, testimony from Mar

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:21.834
a Lago employees.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:22.668
Again, Donald Trump

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:23.703
wants to make this about anything

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:24.170
but him

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:24.871
and the people around

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:25.738
him, that this is him

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:26.606
and the people around him.

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:27.206
I want to quickly

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:28.274
talk about what we just heard

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:28.941
from Jack Smith, though,

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:29.809
because we've

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.377
never heard his voice before.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:32.578
He took this job

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.647
and he is now bringing a historic case

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:35.815
against a former president

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:37.016
and a current frontrunner

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.017
for the Republican nomination.

